Apple today <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2026/03/apple-introduces-the-new-macbook-air-with-m5/">announced</a> refreshed <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macbook-air/">MacBook Air</a> models featuring the M5 chip and a higher base SSD capacity.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2025/03/M4-MacBook-Air-13-and-15-inch-Feature-Pink-and-Teal.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-994261" /><br/>
The M5 chip in the &zwnj;MacBook Air&zwnj; features a 10-core CPU, with what Apple calls the world's fastest CPU cores. It offers configurations with up to 10 GPU cores with Neural Accelerators in each core, delivering up to 4x faster performance for AI tasks than the &zwnj;MacBook Air&zwnj; with the M4 chip.<br/>
<br/>
The chip also has enhanced shader cores and a third-generation ray-tracing engine, along with faster unified memory with 153GB/s of bandwidth, which is a 28% improvement over the M4.<br/>
<br/>
